{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","is_bot":false,"login":"rrnewton","name":"Ryan Newton"},"baseRefName":"main","baseRefOid":"8255986391593432a8f96a38b7b2a6fc02bfc674","body":"[hermit2, cleanup-3, claude-opus-5, devbig014, role=impl]\n\n## Plain Language Summary and Project Impact\n\n`c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/kvm)` has been failing since 2026-09-16,\nwhich fails `e2e.manifest_c_programs`, which is a spine node — so it blocks every\nlanding that needs a validation receipt: the reverie pin bump,\nhttps://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3066, and a third landing. This reverts the\nthree lines that caused it.\n\n**Before:** the kvm cell dies with `Signaled { signal: 14 }` and produces no comparison.\n**After:** the cell passes on both backends.\n\n## The cause\n\n`1d9c9094de` \"Preserve the initial thread identity in synchronous tracing\"\n(https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2945) added three lines to\n`init_sync_file_tracing()`. The helper they call is, in full:\n\n```rust\nfn equalize_tracing_thread_number() {\n    // Create an extra, pointless thread just so that our thread number\n    // starts at the same DetTid \"3\" that `init_file_tracing` does.\n    std::thread::spawn(|| {}).join().unwrap();\n}\n```\n\nSo the synchronous verification-logging path now spawns and joins a **host thread**\nduring init. Under KVM with an interval timer the sandbox is killed by SIGALRM:\n`sandbox failed during Run1: Signaled { signal: 14, core_dumped: false }; no guest\ndisposition or comparison was returned`. ptrace is unaffected throughout.\n\n## Located by bisect, confirmed by revert\n\nBisect over the 112 commits between `fe4108174265` (last observed pass, 09-16 17:47)\nand `ebc2a64b4f18` converged in **7 probes with zero untestable**.\n\nA bisect result is a correlation until the revert is tried, so it was tried — at\ncurrent main `8255986391`:\n\n```\nbefore   FAIL c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/kvm)\n         PASS c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/ptrace)\nafter    PASS c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/kvm)\n         PASS c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/ptrace)\n```\n\n## ⚠️ What this revert costs, named rather than discovered later\n\nThe three lines had a legitimate purpose: aligning the initial DetTid baseline for\nsynchronous verification logging with the one `init_file_tracing` produces. **This\nrevert reintroduces that misalignment, and it is determinism-relevant.**\n\nThere is **no test on either side** — the helper has three call sites and zero tests\n— so nothing in the suite guards 2945's intent and nothing will go red to remind\nanyone. That is why the obligation is tracked rather than left to memory:\n\n> TaskGraph `restore-the-dettid-alignment-without-spawning-a-host-thread` (OPEN)\n\n**The defect is in the mechanism, not the goal.** Burning a DetTid by spawning a host\nthread perturbs signal and timer delivery in the KVM sandbox; achieving the same\nalignment without spawning a thread satisfies both. That belongs in tracing init on\nthe determinism path and should be done deliberately, not inside a revert.\n\nThe trade, explicitly: a known, measured, spine-node blocker for a named and tracked\nidentity mismatch. Not for silence.\n\n## Determinism\n\nThis restores the pre-2945 behaviour of `init_sync_file_tracing`. The reintroduced\nDetTid baseline mismatch for synchronous verification logging is stated above and\ntracked; no other determinism behaviour changes.\n\n## Linux Semantics\n\nUnchanged. The removed call spawned and joined a host thread during tracing init; no\nsyscall dispatch, signal handling, or process-model behaviour is authored here.\n\n## Validation\n\nFail-before / pass-after at current main `8255986391`, shown above, on both backends.\nNo assertion, tolerance, cell or case was weakened, retired or deleted — the cell is\ncorrect and it caught a real defect.\n\n## Human Review Required\n\n**Not triggered** against the four `post-facto-review` triggers: no new syscall\nsupport, no Reverie `Tool`/`Guest`/`Backend`/core-API change, no new determinization\nstrategy, no core DetCore scheduling change. It is a three-line revert in CLI tracing\nsetup. Flagging for the reviewer's judgement rather than hiding it: the reintroduced\nDetTid mismatch is determinism-adjacent, which is why it is named above and tracked.\n","comments":[],"commits":[{"authoredDate":"2026-09-18T12:02:10Z","authors":[{"email":"rrnewton@gmail.com","id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI3NDU4Mg==","login":"rrnewton","name":"Ryan Newton"}],"committedDate":"2026-09-18T12:02:10Z","messageBody":"…under KVM\n\n[hermit2, cleanup-3, claude-opus-5, devbig014, role=impl]\n\nReverts the three lines added to init_sync_file_tracing() by 1d9c9094de\n\"Preserve the initial thread identity in synchronous tracing\"\n(https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/2945), which made\nc-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/kvm) fail.\n\nThe helper those lines call is, in full:\n\n    fn equalize_tracing_thread_number() {\n        // Create an extra, pointless thread just so that our thread number\n        // starts at the same DetTid \"3\" that `init_file_tracing` does.\n        std::thread::spawn(|| {}).join().unwrap();\n    }\n\nso the synchronous verification-logging path spawned and joined a HOST THREAD\nduring init. Under KVM with an interval timer the sandbox is then killed by\nSIGALRM: \"sandbox failed during Run1: Signaled { signal: 14, core_dumped:\nfalse }; no guest disposition or comparison was returned\". ptrace is unaffected.\n\nLOCATED BY BISECT, CONFIRMED BY REVERT. Bisect over the 112 commits between\nfe4108174265 (last observed pass, 2026-09-16 17:47) and ebc2a64b4f18 converged\nin 7 probes with zero untestable. A bisect result is a correlation until the\nrevert is tried, so it was tried, at current main 8255986391:\n\n    before   FAIL c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/kvm)\n             PASS c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/ptrace)\n    after    PASS c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/kvm)\n             PASS c-programs/setitimer-determinism (verify/ptrace)\n\n⚠️ THIS REVERT REINTRODUCES A REAL MISMATCH AND THE COST IS NAMED RATHER THAN\nDISCOVERED LATER. The three lines had a legitimate purpose: aligning the initial\nDetTid baseline for synchronous verification logging with the baseline\ninit_file_tracing produces. Removing them restores that misalignment, which is\ndeterminism-relevant. There is no test on either side -- the helper has three\ncall sites and zero tests -- so nothing in the suite guards 2945's intent, and\nnothing will go red to remind anyone.\n\nThe obligation is tracked rather than left to memory:\nTaskGraph restore-the-dettid-alignment-without-spawning-a-host-thread (OPEN).\n\nThe defect is in the MECHANISM, not the goal. Burning a DetTid by spawning a\nhost thread perturbs signal and timer delivery in the KVM sandbox; achieving the\nsame alignment without spawning a thread would satisfy both. That change belongs\nin tracing init on the determinism path and should be made deliberately, not as\npart of a revert.\n\nTrade being made, explicitly: a known, measured blocker on\ne2e.manifest_c_programs -- which gates the reverie pin bump,\nhttps://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3066 and a third landing -- for a named\nand tracked identity mismatch. Not for silence.\n\nNo assertion, tolerance, cell or case was weakened, retired or deleted. The cell\nis correct and it caught a real defect.","messageHeadline":"Revert the synchronous-tracing thread equalizer that kills setitimer …","oid":"d9d8d32f9511911ef9becac0220bc5d748a414c2"}],"createdAt":"2026-09-18T12:03:24Z","files":[{"path":"hermit-cli/src/bin/hermit/tracing.rs","additions":0,"deletions":3,"changeType":"MODIFIED"}],"headRefName":"revert/sync-tracing-thread-equalizer","headRefOid":"d9d8d32f9511911ef9becac0220bc5d748a414c2","mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","mergeable":"MERGEABLE","reviewDecision":"","reviews":[],"state":"OPEN","statusCheckRollup":[],"title":"Revert the synchronous-tracing thread equalizer that kills setitimer under KVM","updatedAt":"2026-09-18T12:03:24Z","url":"https://github.com/rrnewton/hermit/pull/3096"}
